      "study_window_sharpe_se": 0.46087648000040704,
      "max_drawdown": [
        -0.22464589979062355,
        -0.21485560176954843
      ],
      "reading": "no. On the full post-warmup sample the scaled portfolio is worse; on the study window it is indistinguishable. Neither difference is large against a Sharpe standard error of this size. This lands with Cederburg, O'Doherty, Wang and Yan (2020) rather than with Moreira and Muir (2017), and the reason is the leverage cap: the mandate forbids the levered leg that carries the published result."
    }
